From: Armada OS <armada@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: rmi4 - align with jenneron odin-7.1 (touch bring-up)

Wholesale alignment of rmi_i2c.c/rmi_driver.c/rmi_driver.h with
gitlab.com/jenneron/linux odin-7.1 — the driver state the working pmOS
AYN Odin port actually runs — replacing our older-generation
0030/0033 combination. Key differences that made our touch NAK
(rmi_set_page: set page failed: -6):
 - no reset-gpio handling: 0030 acquired reset-gpios with
   GPIOD_OUT_HIGH (logical active; the line is GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW), i.e.
   probe held the controller IN RESET, hence the I2C NAK. The current
   port leaves the controller as the bootloader left it, with the
   ts_reset_active pinctrl keeping the line released.
 - DRM panel-follower support for suspend/resume tied to panel
   prepare/unprepare (pairs with panel = <&display_panel> in the DTS).
Also re-applies our irq-read error silencing (was 0032).
Replaces 0030-input-rmi4-add-reset-gpio.patch,
0032-rmi4-silence-spam-irq-errors.patch and
0033-input-rmi4-i2c-drm-panel-follower.patch in the series.

